{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/caller.cljc; rg -n 'readiness-attempt-without|caller/close\"'!|closed'\"\\\\?' test/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/responder_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve.caller\n     2\t  \"Call-out readiness at the calling peer: the composition step that\n     3\t   makes a remote call pair ready for a VM before the VM is built.\n     4\t\n     5\t   A VM built over a supplied call pair needs its call-out cursor at\n     6\t   construction (`yin.vm/empty-state` refuses a supplied `:call-out`\n     7\t   without `:call-out-cursor`). Over reflections of a served endpoint\n     8\t   that cursor is a remote answer: the reflection's first `cursor`\n     9\t   answers retry while its request crosses, and only a later ask, after\n    10\t   the drive owner has moved the channel, finds the answer filed. The VM\n    11\t   must not learn that cadence -- readiness belongs to the driver, not\n    12\t   the stream -- so it lives here, in the caller's composition.\n    13\t\n    14\t   `open` attaches both reflections of an apply endpoint and checks the\n    15\t   caller token. `step` asks the call-out reflection once for a\n    16\t   `:dao.stream/newest` cursor: the cursor lands after every response\n    17\t   already on the shared stream, so this caller reads only responses to\n    18\t   requests it sends afterwards. `step` yields `::pending` on retry or\n    19\t   blocked, `::ready` with the minted cursor once it is filed, and is\n    20\t   terminal (`::refused`, `::exhausted`) otherwise; `::max-attempts`\n    21\t   bounds the asks. The drive owner steps its channel between steps.\n    22\t   `vm-opts` then answers the construction options -- the pair, the\n    23\t   cursor, and the caller token -- for any VM's `create-vm`.\n    24\t\n    25\t   Every reflection this step acquires is either handed to a VM\n    26\t   composition through `vm-opts` or closed: a call-out that does not\n    27\t   attach closes the call-in already attached, and `step` closes both\n    28\t   when it ends `::refused` or `::exhausted`. A ready caller whose owner\n    29\t   builds no VM is torn down with `close!`. A reflection's close is\n    30\t   local, and it releases the reflection's outstanding and pending work.\n    31\t\n    32\t   The caller value is a plain value threaded by its owner; nothing here\n    33\t   loops, waits or reads a clock.\"\n    34\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n    35\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n    36\t            [yin.vm :as vm]))\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t(def default-max-attempts\n    40\t  \"How many cursor asks `step` makes before it gives up as `::exhausted`.\"\n    41\t  16)\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\t(defn- refused\n    45\t  [option reason]\n    46\t  {::status ::refused, ::refusals [{::option option, ::reason reason}]})\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\t(defn- attach\n    50\t  [attach! descriptor]\n    51\t  (let [r (try (attach! descriptor)\n    52\t               (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))]\n    53\t    (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n    54\t      (:dao.stream/handle r))))\n    55\t\n    56\t\n    57\t(defn- close-quietly\n    58\t  \"Close reflection `h`. Close is idempotent and total over ok; a\n    59\t   handle that throws on close has nothing left to release here.\"\n    60\t  [h]\n    61\t  (try (stream/close! h)\n    62\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n    63\t\n    64\t\n    65\t(defn close!\n    66\t  \"Tear down a caller whose readiness ends without a VM: close both\n    67\t   reflections it holds, once. Idempotent; a caller refused at `open`\n    68\t   holds none. Returns the caller, `::closed? true`, which `vm-opts`\n    69\t   no longer answers for. `step` calls this itself on its terminal\n    70\t   failures; a caller whose pair went to a VM must not be closed here --\n    71\t   the VM composition owns those reflections.\"\n    72\t  [caller]\n    73\t  (if (or (::closed? caller) (nil? (::call-in caller)))\n    74\t    caller\n    75\t    (do (close-quietly (::call-in caller))\n    76\t        (close-quietly (::call-out caller))\n    77\t        (assoc caller ::closed? true))))\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\t(defn- portable-id?\n    81\t  \"True when the call ids this caller mints survive `codec` -- encoded,\n    82\t   decoded back. No codec asserts nothing more than plain data.\"\n    83\t  [codec caller-id]\n    84\t  (let [id [caller-id :parked-0]]\n    85\t    (or (nil? codec)\n    86\t        (try (= id ((:decode codec) ((:encode codec) id)))\n    87\t             (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ false)))))\n    88\t\n    89\t\n    90\t(defn open\n    91\t  \"Attach the call pair of apply `::endpoint` through `::attach!` (the\n    92\t   caller's attacher, `(fn [descriptor] -> attach outcome)`), for the\n    93\t   caller tenure named by `::caller-id` -- a token the composition mints,\n    94\t   unique per tenure (`yin.vm/ffi-caller-id?`). Optional:\n    95\t   `::max-attempts` (default `default-max-attempts`), and `::codec`, the\n    96\t   channel codec `{:encode f :decode f}` the call ids must survive.\n    97\t\n    98\t   Returns the caller value, `::status ::pending`, or\n    99\t   `{::status ::refused ::refusals [...]}` before anything is attached\n   100\t   when an option is malformed, or naming the reflection that did not\n   101\t   attach.\"\n   102\t  [opts]\n   103\t  (let [{::keys [endpoint attach! caller-id max-attempts codec]} opts\n   104\t        max-attempts (or max-attempts default-max-attempts)]\n   105\t    (cond\n   106\t      (not (fn? attach!)) (refused ::attach! ::malformed)\n   107\t      (not (apply2/endpoint? endpoint)) (refused ::endpoint ::malformed)\n   108\t      (not (vm/ffi-caller-id? caller-id)) (refused ::caller-id ::malformed)\n   109\t      (not (portable-id? codec caller-id)) (refused ::caller-id ::unportable)\n   110\t      (not (and (int? max-attempts) (pos? max-attempts)))\n   111\t      (refused ::max-attempts ::malformed)\n   112\t      :else\n   113\t      (if-some [in (attach attach! (apply2/endpoint-request endpoint))]\n   114\t        (if-some [out (attach attach! (apply2/endpoint-response endpoint))]\n   115\t          {::status ::pending,\n   116\t           ::call-in in,\n   117\t           ::call-out out,\n   118\t           ::caller-id caller-id,\n   119\t           ::attempts 0,\n   120\t           ::max-attempts max-attempts}\n   121\t          (do (close-quietly in)\n   122\t              (refused ::call-out ::unattached)))\n   123\t        (refused ::call-in ::unattached)))))\n   124\t\n   125\t\n   126\t(defn step\n   127\t  \"Ask the call-out reflection once for a `:dao.stream/newest` cursor.\n   128\t   `ok` makes the caller `::ready` with that cursor; retry or blocked\n   129\t   leaves it `::pending`, or `::exhausted` once `::max-attempts` asks\n   130\t   have gone unanswered; any other outcome refuses it with that\n   131\t   `::outcome`. Both terminal failures close the caller's reflections\n   132\t   (`close!`). A caller that is not pending is returned unchanged.\"\n   133\t  [caller]\n   134\t  (if-not (= ::pending (::status caller))\n   135\t    caller\n   136\t    (let [r (stream/cursor (::call-out caller) stream/anchor-newest)\n   137\t          o (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   138\t          attempts (inc (::attempts caller))]\n   139\t      (cond\n   140\t        (= :dao.stream/ok o)\n   141\t        (assoc caller\n   142\t               ::status ::ready\n   143\t               ::attempts attempts\n   144\t               ::call-out-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   145\t        (or (= :dao.stream/blocked o) (:dao.stream/retry? r))\n   146\t        (if (< attempts (::max-attempts caller))\n   147\t          (assoc caller ::attempts attempts)\n   148\t          (close! (assoc caller ::status ::exhausted ::attempts attempts)))\n   149\t        :else (close! (assoc caller\n   150\t                             ::status ::refused\n   151\t                             ::attempts attempts\n   152\t                             ::outcome o))))))\n   153\t\n   154\t\n   155\t(defn ready?\n   156\t  \"True when the caller holds a minted cursor and was not torn down.\"\n   157\t  [caller]\n   158\t  (and (= ::ready (::status caller)) (not (::closed? caller))))\n   159\t\n   160\t\n   161\t(defn call-out-cursor\n   162\t  \"The minted call-out cursor of a ready caller, else nil.\"\n   163\t  [caller]\n   164\t  (when (ready? caller) (::call-out-cursor caller)))\n   165\t\n   166\t\n   167\t(defn vm-opts\n   168\t  \"The construction options a ready caller hands any VM's `create-vm`:\n   169\t   `:call-in`, `:call-out`, `:call-out-cursor` and `:ffi-caller-id`.\n   170\t   nil when the caller is not ready.\"\n   171\t  [caller]\n   172\t  (when (ready? caller)\n   173\t    {:call-in (::call-in caller),\n   174\t     :call-out (::call-out caller),\n   175\t     :call-out-cursor (::call-out-cursor caller),\n   176\t     :ffi-caller-id (::caller-id caller)}))\n964:(defn- closed?\n982:(deftest a-readiness-attempt-without-a-vm-leaves-no-open-reflection\n1004:        (is (every? closed? @acquired))))\n1010:        (is (true? (::caller/closed? c)))\n1013:        (is (every? closed? @acquired))))\n1023:        (is (true? (::caller/closed? c)))\n1025:        (is (every? closed? @acquired))))\n1029:            closed (caller/close! ready)]\n1031:        (is (nil? (::caller/closed? ready)) \"readiness alone closes nothing\")\n1034:        (is (every? closed? @acquired))\n1035:        (is (= closed (caller/close! closed)) \"a second close! is a no-op\")\n1036:        (is (= closed (caller/close! (caller/close! closed))))))\n1039:        (is (= r (caller/close! r)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
